Cell[TextData[{
 "Next we calculate the Eigensystem of the matrix ",
 StyleBox["dnm. ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "Mathematica lists the Eigensystem of a matrix in the descending order of \
the eigenvalues. But in the case of a Hamiltonian we want them in ascending \
order. \nThe resulting numerically approximated eigenstates ",
 StyleBox["EigenState[r_][x_]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " are still continuous functions on the real axis."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.992573034967477*^9, 3.9925730760105124`*^9}, {
   3.992573245746047*^9, 3.992573297969474*^9}, {3.992573375103759*^9, 
   3.992573444666151*^9}, {3.99257384784009*^9, 3.992573893912764*^9}, 
   3.992574048682549*^9, 3.992574081843865*^9, {3.992575101736039*^9, 
